    "body": "Found during the #108 review (Tier 2). Pre-existing on `main`.\n\n### Problem\n`HiveConnectorFactory::locations` (`crates/hive/src/datasource.rs`) caches table storage locations keyed by **table name only**, not `catalog.schema.table`. Within one Arneb process, whichever of two same-named tables in different schemas is read first wins, and queries against the other one **silently read the first table's files**.\n\n### Repro\nWith both `hive.tpch.orders` (DOUBLE) and `hive.tpch_decimal.orders` (DECIMAL) seeded (`docker compose run --rm tpch-seed` and `TPCH_DECIMAL=1 docker compose run --rm tpch-seed`):\n1. In one Arneb process, query `tpch.orders` (e.g. `SELECT avg(o_totalprice) FROM datalake.tpch.orders`).\n2. Then query `datalake.tpch_decimal.orders` with the same aggregate.\n3. The second result comes from the first table's files (wrong types/values); in a fresh process the order flips which one is wrong. It first looked like a \"flaky\" DECIMAL AVG.\n\n### Impact\nSilent wrong results whenever two schemas (or catalogs) contain tables with the same name — common in real data lakes (`staging.orders` / `prod.orders`, per-tenant schemas). Also affects Iceberg tables redirected through the Hive catalog if they share a name with a Hive table elsewhere.\n\n### Fix direction\nKey the cache by the fully qualified `(catalog, schema, table)` (and consider invalidation when HMS metadata changes). Add a test with two same-named tables in different schemas read in one process.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
